# Head of the Hunt: "If a creature an opponent controls would die, exile it instead. When you do, create a 2/2 green Wolf creature
# token." Bot1's Lightning Bolt destroys Bot2's Ornithopter: it is exiled, not put into the graveyard, and Bot1 gets a Wolf from the
# reflexive trigger (on the stack above nothing: Stack.Count is 1 when it is put there). Bot2 has nothing in its graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Black Lotus
Head of the Hunt
Lightning Bolt
Plains x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Plains x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Head of the Hunt.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Exile = Ornithopter
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Wolf Token.Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Wolf Token.Colors = Green
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 3
Stack.Count = 0
